        { "$comment": "P69 (lane cs): `naked`, in either spelling — a function whose body is its whole code, with no prologue and no epilogue. MEASURED: gcc 13.3.0 and clang 18.1.3 on x86_64 Linux, Apple clang on arm64 and mingw-w64 gcc all honour the GNU spelling (a body that is only assembly returns its value), mingw-w64 gcc the `__declspec` one too, and gcc on arm64 Linux ignores it with a warning. This compiler always emits the frame, so a naked function's own return would run inside it: refused by name until the function emitter learns to emit none.", "names": ["naked_"], "effect": "unsupported", "reason": "it asks for a function with no prologue and no epilogue, whose body is its whole code, and this compiler always emits both" },
